From e01026c7d41abf584cde32503bc6356295d9314a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dj <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:34:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] net: apple: Add T6050 N1 firmware and ACIPC transport

Boot the N1 firmware and expose its shared ACIPC transport behind the T6050 PCIe host. After the ROM boot, isolate and quiesce function 0, put it in D3hot with PME enabled, let the host's root-port reset take the link through L2, PERST# and retraining, then restore the root port's and the endpoint's state. Keep firmware and calibration as external inputs, and retain supplier lifetime for the separate Wi-Fi and Bluetooth consumers.

Source snapshot: t6050-gpu ee68abb105200e99636a5edfc647a5cfc1d89954
Integration base: 9cbdd0734d9e186c5f5f5949a21b909d10c2571b

Signed-off-by: Dj <hey@djdev.me>
Co-developed-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>

(cherry picked from commit de6d28883375bfadf63ca4559247b41dd148385f)
[n1-wifi: on aurora-j716s this driver replaces integration's J813/J873 N1 driver files]
